{"name":"Sunny Festival","hex":"#ffc946","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sunny","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Featuring a lot of sunshine.","Receiving a lot of sunshine."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["sunny side up"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunny"},{"term":"festival","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to a feast or feast day; festive."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A feast or feast day, now especially a special event or series of events celebrating such occasions.","An event or series of special events centred on the celebration or promotion of some theme or aspect of the community, often held at regular intervals."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/festival"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunny (2011 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sunny (Korean: 써니) is a 2011 South Korean comedy-drama film. The film is about a middle-aged woman who tries to fulfill her friend's dying wish of reuniting their group of high school friends. The film alternates between two timelines: the present day where the women are middle-aged, and the 1980s when they were in high school. It is the second film by writer-director Kang Hyeong-cheol, who previously directed Scandal Makers (2008)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b4/Sunny2011filmposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunny_(2011_film)","wikidata":"Q492504"},{"title":"Sunny (manga)","blocks":[{"text":"Sunny is a Japanese manga series written and illustrated by Taiyō Matsumoto. It was serialized in Shogakukan's seinen manga magazine Monthly Ikki from December 2010 to September 2014, when the magazine ceased publication. It was later transferred to Monthly Big Comic Spirits, being serialized from January to July 2015. Its chapters were collected in six wide-ban volumes. The manga was licensed for English release in North America by Viz Media. In April 2025, an anime film adaptation produced by Dwarf Studios was announced, which is slated for completion in 2029."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/79/Sunny_by_Taiyo_Matsumoto_v1_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunny_(manga)","wikidata":"Q18154676"},{"title":"Festival","blocks":[{"text":"A festival is an event celebrated by a community and centred on one or more characteristic aspects of its religion, traditions or cultures. It is often observed as an indigenous or national holiday, a religious celebration, or a cultural fair (mela). A festival is a typical case of glocalization, and also reflects the high culture-low culture interrelationship. In addition to religion and folklore, a significant source for festivals has been agriculture. Since, food is such an essential resource, many festivals are associated with harvest time. Religious observances and thanksgiving for good harvests are integrated into celebrations that take place in autumn, such as Halloween in the northern hemisphere and Easter in the southern hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Holi_Festival_of_Colors_Utah%2C_United_States_2013.jpg/330px-Holi_Festival_of_Colors_Utah%2C_United_States_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Festival","wikidata":"Q132241"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Weezer_Bethlehem_2019_5.jpg/500px-Weezer_Bethlehem_2019_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Weezer_Bethlehem_2019_5.jpg/1280px-Weezer_Bethlehem_2019_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Weezer_Bethlehem_2019_